From: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Subject: mm/mempolicy: use one node set for interleave weights
Date: Sun Oct 25 01:03:44 PM PDT 2026

Switching weighted interleave back to automatic mode while memory is being
onlined can cause a kernel divide error on x86, and a panic if
panic_on_oops is set.

reduce_interleave_weights() scans N_MEMORY three times.  Its caller holds
wi_state_lock, which protects the bandwidth table and weights but does not
prevent memory hotplug from changing N_MEMORY.  If the first pass sums
zero bandwidth, a returning node with previously recorded positive
bandwidth can enter the next pass and cause a division by zero.

Record the nodes visited while summing their bandwidth, then use that same
set when scaling and reducing the weights.  The arithmetic remains
consistent even if hotplug changes N_MEMORY during the first pass.  This
needs no additional locking and remains usable from hotplug callbacks.

Fixes: e341f9c3c841 ("mm/mempolicy: Weighted Interleave Auto-tuning")
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: "Gregory Price (Meta)" <gourry@gourry.net>
Cc: <stable@vger.kernel.org>
---

 mm/mempolicy.c |   13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/mm/mempolicy.c~mm-mempolicy-use-one-node-set-for-interleave-weights
+++ a/mm/mempolicy.c
@@ -207,15 +207,22 @@ static u8 get_il_weight(int node)
  */
 static void reduce_interleave_weights(unsigned int *bw, u8 *new_iw)
 {
+	nodemask_t nodes = NODE_MASK_NONE;
 	u64 sum_bw = 0;
 	unsigned int cast_sum_bw, scaling_factor = 1, iw_gcd = 0;
 	int nid;
 
-	for_each_node_state(nid, N_MEMORY)
+	/*
+	 * N_MEMORY can change while wi_state_lock is held. Remember the
+	 * nodes contributing to sum_bw so all passes use the same set.
+	 */
+	for_each_node_state(nid, N_MEMORY) {
+		node_set(nid, nodes);
 		sum_bw += bw[nid];
+	}
 
 	/* Scale bandwidths to whole numbers in the range [1, weightiness] */
-	for_each_node_state(nid, N_MEMORY) {
+	for_each_node_mask(nid, nodes) {
 		/*
 		 * Try not to perform 64-bit division.
 		 * If sum_bw < scaling_factor, then sum_bw < U32_MAX.
@@ -234,7 +241,7 @@ static void reduce_interleave_weights(un
 	}
 
 	/* 1:2 is strictly better than 16:32. Reduce by the weights' GCD. */
-	for_each_node_state(nid, N_MEMORY)
+	for_each_node_mask(nid, nodes)
 		new_iw[nid] /= iw_gcd;
 }
 
_
